#: ../../howto/local-a2a.rst:4
msgid "Local A2A endpoint"
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/local-a2a.rst:9
msgid ""
"Every node serves the A2A protocol on a loopback address. Each remote "
"agent on the network appears there as an ordinary A2A server, with its "
"own URL and its own agent card. A client that speaks A2A, such as an "
"agent framework, a coding tool, or a script that uses an A2A SDK, "
"therefore reaches the network without any ANet-specific code and without "
"running an HTTPS server of its own."
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/local-a2a.rst:16
msgid ""
"This page describes how a client finds the endpoint and authenticates, "
"which routes and operations exist, what the proxy card contains, and how "
"the same module forwards tasks that arrive at the node to a local A2A "
"server."
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/local-a2a.rst:26
msgid "Concept"
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/local-a2a.rst:28
msgid ""
"The local interface is the module ``a2a``. It is enabled by default and "
"needs no configuration block; ``anet init`` does not write one. It is the"
" way ANet contributes to A2A instead of competing with it: tasks are A2A "
"tasks, cards are A2A agent cards, and payments follow the a2a-x402 "
"extension. What lies behind the card, which is end-to-end encryption "
"through a hub that sees no content, identities with key histories, "
"receipts, and payments, is the business of the daemon. It reaches the "
"client only as A2A objects and as metadata with the prefix ``anet.``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/local-a2a.rst:37
msgid "Properties of the interface:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/local-a2a.rst:39
msgid ""
"**One path per remote agent.** A client that holds the URL of one agent "
"and the local token reaches the tasks of that agent and no others. The "
"node is not a remote agent of itself, and requests for its own AID are "
"answered with \"no such agent\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/local-a2a.rst:43
msgid ""
"**Loopback only, with a token of its own.** The token of this interface "
"(``a2a_token.txt``) is separate from the control token of the node. It "
"authorizes less: tasks as a requester and payments within the agent tier."
" The control token is not accepted here, and this token is not accepted "
"on the control plane."
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/local-a2a.rst:48
msgid ""
"**Requester side.** The interface sends tasks to remote agents. Whether "
"the remote node takes a task is decided by that node; a new node accepts "
"no task from a stranger."
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/local-a2a.rst:51
msgid ""
"**No push notifications.** The cards declare ``pushNotifications: "
"false``. A client that is not connected cannot be reached by the "
"interface."
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/local-a2a.rst:56
msgid "Address and token"
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/local-a2a.rst:58
msgid ""
"The interface writes two files to its state directory, ``<data "
"directory>/modules/a2a/``. The default data directory is ``~/.anet``; the"
" environment variable ``ANET_DATA_DIR`` selects another one."
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/local-a2a.rst:62
msgid "``a2a_addr.txt``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/local-a2a.rst:63
msgid ""
"The address ``host:port`` of the listener. The port is chosen from the "
"range 43811 to 45810 the first time the interface starts, and it is "
"recorded and bound again on every later start. Clients are configured "
"with this address, so it must not change between starts."
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/local-a2a.rst:68
msgid "``a2a_token.txt``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/local-a2a.rst:69
msgid ""
"The bearer token. It is created once and stored with a private mode. The "
"token changes when the address changes, when the daemon rotates its local"
" credentials, and after an emergency key rotation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/local-a2a.rst:73
msgid "A client reads both files when it is configured:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/local-a2a.rst:82
msgid ""
"The function ``auth`` supplies the header through a file descriptor, so "
"that the token does not appear in the argument list of ``curl``, which "
"other users of the machine can read with ``ps``. The examples below use "
"it in bash or zsh."
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/local-a2a.rst:87
msgid "Port conflicts"
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/local-a2a.rst:89
msgid ""
"If another process holds the recorded port when the daemon starts, the "
"interface does not move to another port. Clients that were configured "
"with the old address would continue to send the token to whichever "
"process holds that port. Instead the interface stays down, the rest of "
"the node keeps running, and the daemon writes the file "
"``a2a_port_conflict.txt`` in the state directory and to its log. When the"
" holder may belong to another local user, the token is replaced as well."
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/local-a2a.rst:97
msgid ""
"``anet up`` and ``anet doctor`` report the conflict. The remedy is to "
"free the port, restart the node, and then update the clients:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/local-a2a.rst:105
msgid ""
"The second command rewrites the ``a2a_agents`` entries of Hermes; clients"
" that are configured in another way are updated by the operator with the "
"new address and token."
msgstr ""

